<newsitem itemid="30632" id="root" date="1996-09-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: IMI profits boosted by exceptional gain.</title>
<headline>IMI profits boosted by exceptional gain.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		31.1		   vs 9.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.0		    vs 4.6</p>
<p> Pretax		     138.0		  vs 49.0</p>
<p> Exceptional gain	 70.8		   vs nil</p>
<p> Profit before exceptional items 67.2	vs 49.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pretax, preexceptional profits were in a range of 64 to 70 million stg.  </p>
<p> Turnover		   690		    vs 669</p>
<p> Operating result	 68.4		   vs 52.1</p>
<p> Interest		   4.4 debit	    vs 4.6 debit</p>
<p> Tax			  30.9		   vs 18.1</p>
<p> Pay date		   Oct 14</p>
<p> Div registration date  Sept 17</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Sept 9</p>
<p>NOTE - IMI Plc is an engineering firm. The exceptional gain stems from several disposals.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
